{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"ada9eb9c192de5db1ec005b3917749b1f458d996bd5032e27920a595ede028af","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T10:23:06Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[222,223]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","quoted_text":"        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=qcow2\" % (run / \"overlay.qcow2\"),\n        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=raw,readonly=on\" % (run / \"seed.iso\"),","reason":"qemu_command interpolates the resolved run path directly into QEMU's -drive file= option. QEMU treats commas as option separators, so a state directory containing a comma produces malformed drive arguments for overlay.qcow2 and seed.iso. This is a routine correctness defect; escaping embedded commas in the file values or rejecting such state paths is the smallest compatible fix.","target":"fdf8d470f0eb1c53065cc9d815b366b6f4c2e41e"},"finding_id":"9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568","previous_event_id":"ecaeadf18f31cab802326fdbd0e120e86c1ec4d6dffd31dda4df5bb19cc4f311","review_id":"f1b5131645f96822be0f07c1707f2cbcab3333693f6cab11de508eb6e932b92d"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568:67b4125da0a3c9a2c1e354475743033e07bfdd0c4f3790cf8949c9191961cf2e"}